{
  "case_id": "2009-08-970",
  "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:10 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plaintiff's counsel in this case earned a large fee award based on prevailing market hourly rates and a substantial number of hours expended. However, the district court determined that the $6 million lodestar was insufficient to compensate them for the quality of their representation or their results obtained."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm sorry. Could you repeat what the market was? Was it the market for all attorneys or only for attorneys doing this type of work?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The lawyer doesn't get a fee in a fee-shifting statute if he loses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1988 permits reasonable attorney's fees. That means going above and beyond the lodestar amount can be justified only if the lodestar is unreasonably low. We submit that a lodestar based on prevailing market rates does not require a performance bonus on top of the lodestar to make an award reasonable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You are saying we can never exceed the lodestar amount? I mean, we have said in some cases that in extraordinary circumstances it can. What are those extraordinary circumstances, or do you think there are none?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shah",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHAH: Your Honor, I think the limited\ncircumstances which allow for a downward adjustment\nwould be those set forth in this Court's decision in\nHensley. I don't think that poor performance alone\nwould justify a downward departure --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: For extraordinary circumstances, what about a very, very popular cause and he wins and they are beating his door down? Can we reduce it for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They call these partial contingency or\nhybrid contingency arrangements. It's not the same\nstandard hourly rate and then a client decides to throw\nin a kicker of a million dollar bonus. Rather, these\nare discounted rates with a success bonus, essentially a\nmodified form of contingency arrangement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What is the overhead?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: So you want this Court to look to those cases -- you know, it's the world turned upside down. Instead of the lower courts reading our cases, we have to read lower court cases to decide what this statute means. Is that it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that says, the lodestar is not just a guiding principle but is an absolute ceiling on the award."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask this one final question: We have a question of law before us, whether there\u2019s an absolute ceiling here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR COHEN",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. COHEN: We are arguing that the enhancement in this case was unreasonable, Your Honor, and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-970",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "b321065cff0ebec2400cd7aae84723b582ab60a12d5f627e3e259806c75b0c2a",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b321065cff0e-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
